35,2,1,talk,Toshio,,The post-occupancy data is clear. Shared spaces rated highest; single-wing projects disappointed users. I will check the survey findings next.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Victoria,,"The timetable records are troubling. Every room closed for works required hired off-site space, paid for over two terms.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,George,,The staffing freeze left grounds posts empty. Technicians still do manual window checks weekly. The burden is on the few remaining.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Mizuki,,The delivery data is damning. Inspection-driven works hit deadlines; comfort projects slipped a year. The weather diaries confirm six weeks lost to rain.,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,The reserve is empty. Equipment costs are hidden until they explode. Tender data shows plant costs up twenty percent. The market is correcting our optimism.,"{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Toshio,,"@Benjamin, the reserve gap is critical. My survey data shows hazardous material in older blocks. That adds months before work starts.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Victoria,,"@Toshio, that hazardous material finding explains the delays. My booking data shows specialist rooms are idle, yet general rooms are always full.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,George,,"@Victoria, idle specialist rooms mean less daily maintenance. That is a relief for the remaining staff.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Mizuki,,"@Toshio, hazardous material is a classic unpriced snag. It validates my concern about the calendar slipping. We must avoid those older blocks.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Mizuki, exactly. The market is punishing our optimism. We need a plan that doesn’t rely on outdated equipment or hidden reserves.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Toshio,,The survey confirms the risk. Older blocks are traps. We must avoid them to protect the schedule and the budget.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Victoria,,"@George, the idle specialist rooms are a waste. We should repurpose them for the general demand that is currently being turned away.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,George,,"@Victoria, repurposing adds new routines. The technicians are already drowning in manual checks. We cannot add to their load.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Mizuki,,"@George, I agree. Adding routines to an exhausted team is a recipe for failure. We need a plan that respects their current limits.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,"@Victoria, repurposing sounds efficient, but it ignores the maintenance burden. We cannot trade one hidden cost for another.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
